[{"id":"VRCE-6-15-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":1,"english":"Then from forth the mid-sea arose Ocean himself, even as the maker of day rise from the mighty ascending-hill, Meru. And accompanied by Pannagas* of flaming faces, the Ocean showed himself, appearing like cool lapises, adorned with golden ornaments, wearing a wreath of gems and a jewelled vesture, with his eyes resembling lotus-leaves, bearing on his head a noble garland containing all flowers; decked with ornaments of polished gold; as well with excellent ornaments of gems originating in himself, like the mountains Himavān embellished with metals (sprung in himself).-(the Ocean arose) with wave on wave whirling around, and rife with winds blowing among clouds, surrounded by streams, Gangā, Sindhu (and others). *Semi-divine serpents.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-14","DUTT-6-22-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1da247e136d64f1000c41ba0f1b8001f011ef834ffed987f7285893bd97240f9","compact":"20e941fe5b8552c7beef374144a0575b3ceeb41c70f3e4855f53685e1232caad","nasal":"53408dd3add748513e99595997ab8ab21d0b059db2c9b56c72a5ed2b37f497b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":2,"english":"And accompanied by Pannagas* of flaming faces, the Ocean showed himself, appearing like cool lapises, adorned with golden ornaments, wearing a wreath of gems and a jewelled vesture, with his eyes resembling lotus-leaves, bearing on his head a noble garland containing all flowers; decked with ornaments of polished gold; as well with excellent ornaments of gems originating in himself, like the mountains Himavān embellished with metals (sprung in himself).-(the Ocean arose) with wave on wave whirling around, and rife with winds blowing among clouds, surrounded by streams, Gangā, Sindhu (and others). *Semi-divine serpents.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a67c929ff2c52ac17ed09bb6be8d9c649b661527fa6bf3ef658d5c962e11cc5","compact":"36616246fae96cd34b7c11f1438e012cebc48195d01750598ddf5840ed60d8f8","nasal":"f4c0b755c7410f923ef1b53a2d685e33676c404dbfd581a4dd246e68dbf3380b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":3,"english":"And approaching the arrow-showering Rāma, and greeting him fair, Ocean spoke to him with joined hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c0cdf41e90d9f7ee0ee830a233f419ff939b9e01b1c1a8b6570d28bbc1f6e17d","compact":"8bc01417b265bdead5e686d5f69be3ec46c542eb73e71d54e06bb52ffc1d140b","nasal":"618240261cc4693ce560a2fce697d71a25d57f2f20c1dd655ab2d21818dca9bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":4,"english":"O Rāghava, earth, air, sky, water and light, these, O mild one, retaining their eternal course, maintain their (respective) nature.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"240e4a9b78ef0d8a5cb4ca9d43d532036c02c7309b564ddccfbe19eac87b8356","compact":"9ca48e59e2aebcda32c4e67c183f6a17286ceee57403806fd8268560d9731273","nasal":"2ec7a5792291c9ec313e711c28b1f14bb4dac25a2dcd3c977b1722bb92956519"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":5,"english":"Mine also is that nature whereby I am fathomless and incapable of being crossed. The reverse of this is the having a bottom. And for this reason I speak to you (concerning the means).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79d05fbdd575024bcae4cd20a24ac5541db7af3e7897cd2bba3b79c45ceedfc9","compact":"7cc0574bcc7c19b8ef532f5ec3e87c93c786274e70f40978d00e888a07ddd26d","nasal":"7cc0574bcc7c19b8ef532f5ec3e87c93c786274e70f40978d00e888a07ddd26d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":6,"english":"O king's son, not from desire, covetousness, or fear, or anger, can I anywise deprive my waters abounding in alligators of their (perpetual) motion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.678,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3284ecf04a003ebd4e3ff3784cc58aaac300ada18819c0ce66e7e08b9881d8b3","compact":"3a8c1a0007403b5a57f3acf8a10c37d0bc543923829fe2c4534ce2a77ac90931","nasal":"5d6027eb30317e74045a0b343604c6b8f58323577988b741e72e64850930c406"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":7,"english":"I will tell you how you will pass (over me); or and I will bear it. And no ferocious aquatic animals shall do wrong so long as your forces have not crossed. And, O Rāma, I will make as it were firm land for the crossing over of the monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.344,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a15ed0ceea657cd8c9545c6e3d3575b00113a379eff21b1527da0195f6664f78","compact":"75915c63a5976ce6c675f4cffb6483d381cda692d8169a07e922ccb438254587","nasal":"d95b63586bb90a0014d16d2844404e814bc82871a61ac429cfc0e6b12ff0ade5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":8,"english":"O mild one, this one is named Nala, son to Viśvakarmā. He has received a boon from his sire. Visvakarma's son is well pleased with you. Let this monkey, surcharged with exhuberant spirits, build a bridge over me. I will hold that up. This one is as his sire.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.677,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0434e4312b81ff380d67c49fd3b31005463bb95c54de376f0f27af4a52450f4a","compact":"71337dc90e6a270d80e3f0d2a5160611ed5ccc2e4e7bc7e47f680845f1a1635a","nasal":"71337dc90e6a270d80e3f0d2a5160611ed5ccc2e4e7bc7e47f680845f1a1635a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":9,"english":"O mild one, this one is named Nala, son to Viśvakarmā. He has received a boon from his sire. Visvakarma's son is well pleased with you. Let this monkey, surcharged with exhuberant spirits, build a bridge over me. I will hold that up. This one is as his sire.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"25bc4ae948979fdcd9e27a1044ee7855501b2e03794e4a4440d86b77a6be7053","compact":"e2f3067591c4cadd8633200b04cc0a8283ce6ae9e6bf63f00e9ff198b52a1f82","nasal":"e2f3067591c4cadd8633200b04cc0a8283ce6ae9e6bf63f00e9ff198b52a1f82"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":10,"english":"Having delivered himself thus, Ocean disappeared. Then that foremost of monkeys, Nala, arising, spoke to the mighty Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.984,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"71b48e21d2a4a2f3723a4598a7c2236adaac4b2a7b2cff70dffee3fe30f87f21","compact":"a8173153d3cb1b1ccd944851667eb23778d15c0e29009f76adaf48fa2a2a26a6","nasal":"a8173153d3cb1b1ccd944851667eb23778d15c0e29009f76adaf48fa2a2a26a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":11,"english":"Resorting to my sire's skill, I will build a bridge over the spacious abode of Makaras. The mighty Ocean has spoken justly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4efa4e9252b9766d11a24750b5ea83fa22212651015a88b230cae519c5cb0d5b","compact":"b2d24ad156d649c1dc6741b4e744258ad93b88fb1fd6fdfa1d53ba28f1a6bbcc","nasal":"b2d24ad156d649c1dc6741b4e744258ad93b88fb1fd6fdfa1d53ba28f1a6bbcc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":12,"english":"(Formerly) in Mandara, Visvakarma had conferred a boon on my mother: 'O exalted one, your son shall be like me. I am a son of his, sprung from his lions, and I am like to Viśvakarmā. Ocean reminded me all the things. Not having been asked by you, I had not unfolded my qualifications.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.441,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-40","DUTT-6-22-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce87d6bb724b9cfcdda51ca78b45885d0b7aaa6ad111665a109cf91434ce9c91","compact":"b5b9d8ec198711dfee8ad2969779662a3c4960fbd293edd2af53982c5786c9c4","nasal":"8213c7db539a7366e9719cd6a4029e1ce8846da4262604957057420393f5cbff"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":13,"english":"I am a son of his, sprung from his lions, and I am like to Viśvakarmā. Ocean reminded me all the things. Not having been asked by you, I had not unfolded my qualifications. I also am capable of constructing a bridge over Varuna's abode. Therefore this very day let the foremost monkeys construct the bridge.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.359,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-41","DUTT-6-22-42"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a2d6578ec1f431ccec059bff68a6bea49923c0a66fd67e87605f7de12753965b","compact":"e90b3270acd2985ff11084474010e808dc053f537c88fdad6d493d0e410f7d09","nasal":"9ae6fa99fed2a373b08efe07fdb01ef2c0f720138e75ae70b75b0c5f90e8109f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":14,"english":"Then directed by Rāma, the principal monkeys with alacrity entered the mighty forest in hundreds and thousands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90766e4ff750fc6dcea4a9885b731252c96627cd98e1b7781008b2ce4e15e14f","compact":"85b38e5a4372d8a283e9fa3856bddf7c9c56a7f79ba301424a11ba25444e78f1","nasal":"85b38e5a4372d8a283e9fa3856bddf7c9c56a7f79ba301424a11ba25444e78f1"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":15,"english":"Themselves resembling mountains, the foremost of the monkeys began to break down trees and draw them towards the Ocean.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.639,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"049cc74f97214fe64189ecf88598f2a034dadf1a45a154cd9186237c5713dae7","compact":"a33205b95e4920e3069976fb4664a7cebe9545d72ee2dbbf1daec749ee0d2d97","nasal":"1daa7ba4f10f28b2a5839decf6d25ff63bcf8a403476d909a9b79db12ab915fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":16,"english":"The monkeys filled the Ocean with Sālas, and Ašvakarņas, dhavas, bamboo's and kutajas, arjunas, palms, tilakas, tinicas, billakas, saptaparnas, and blossoming karnikāras, mangoes, and asoka trees.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.676,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"023ee3fb33b259be9ba5d61e2289836b60170ca274470b20bac9d2053458ba1c","compact":"6cfc63251f8bd430c341f9428284d4e6b0e184d669e05d904490c734dd19bfa9","nasal":"6cfc63251f8bd430c341f9428284d4e6b0e184d669e05d904490c734dd19bfa9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":17,"english":"The monkeys filled the Ocean with Sālas, and Ašvakarņas, dhavas, bamboo's and kutajas, arjunas, palms, tilakas, tinicas, billakas, saptaparnas, and blossoming karnikāras, mangoes, and asoka trees.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e4140ac45981fee91a9dfcdb327091e7f3f9fa86db01543e944ba35f67bd9edb","compact":"fa0d02040b309493744384e0aac458b707db9961363313d5be1f4903d83c94c3","nasal":"fa0d02040b309493744384e0aac458b707db9961363313d5be1f4903d83c94c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":18,"english":"And those monkeys the foremost of their species-began to gather the trees, some with their roots, and some without them, carrying them like Indra's ensign.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-46"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e305913db604b326404e2ceb215a74d9f06cc34d95a91503969a5c8b37e3e666","compact":"010722b246a89e992068e9944c2ba1271371d795e2ea15094c420f08f22485d1","nasal":"2c4826be5dee45bac476e7f63d21ea07beec84061345501b8c4fddb39ee01508"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":19,"english":"And on rocks being plunged into the waters, the latter, suddenly swelling up, mounted to the welkin, and again subsided.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.464,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-48"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"760e89030083f033a24d035673c417c756e7afa6b6483fa13564abdabcedae81","compact":"cc665a61e76b52291e85f68c6ed4bfe5fb2769db20a3f5ffb4084e3ea3fd8f99","nasal":"cc665a61e76b52291e85f68c6ed4bfe5fb2769db20a3f5ffb4084e3ea3fd8f99"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":20,"english":"And (the trees) dropping (into the deep), vexed it all around. And some took lines (for insuring straightness to the bridge). And at the middle of the lord of rivers and streams, Nala made a grand bridge measuring an hundred Yojanas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.519,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-49"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"690c70dfde476eedcbe9e0992aa463eb59a539ef70fa5d745d481fb8763cfb70","compact":"922058f9dcddc58081e5c5429d6dd62ccc3ef27690da83eaca37c7c857d16f74","nasal":"922058f9dcddc58081e5c5429d6dd62ccc3ef27690da83eaca37c7c857d16f74"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":21,"english":"And tremendous was the tumult that arose of crags thrown and rocks toppled down into the mighty deep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-52"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4917f984f3233055a6052ccccfc23a9254b2d6e4b200f45cb5259983d4ded3ac","compact":"6796246604aa81ebfa246c48028f1015e85c428653c7917fe4378e58bad3861a","nasal":"6845369ecd27161dd49974cdf91cb81c16a43320838d1c7b0f003508eaed818f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":22,"english":"That bridge built by force over the abode of makaras, looked graceful and splendid like the Milky way in the firmament.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-58"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015022","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3678e363f331f8084a1490d9494c4a9f22b9e853479f25beefb9b2775c2cb28e","compact":"9d2210fce32866d3d67339554f7d966071527d0f496a3926b0a9748f799cc1c8","nasal":"a0cc5aa9a36cc572791b9e660e8053a1cb5fdbd9580c7550e64814f438616f0b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-23","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":23,"english":"Then the deities and Gandharvas, the Siddhas and the prime saints, appearing in the heavens, stood there, eager to behold this wonder.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-59"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015023","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c1530dd044faa1d7effc766cc643386f9372081b26887695ebf679638fd198f","compact":"85989fc2d4774e98888228fa8c374e18e41889b61b678f79720157a93a6a7eb0","nasal":"b1e983a50665bf6b5fabe18056290985ad953d9665ec5798fc7c7a273fb81057"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-24","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":24,"english":"The monkeys, leaping and bounding and roaring, as well as all creatures, beheld that building of the bridge the ocean, on inconceivable, and marvellous, displaying skill past thought and capable of making one's hair stand on end.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-61"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015024","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c4c96afaaae7cb29060c33da08448f205db6a6225170896efe4704f63681888","compact":"535fafc0b43243c337227c7f39240ce8e0b228fbfe541eb60a55275bc2f607d4","nasal":"468fab6757d60a0d7e9b56625bb18854059bfce8c0bea74781a74d2d0da7e326"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-25","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":25,"english":"And those thousands of Koțis of exceeding vigour, having constructed the bridge over the ocean, went over to the other shore of the mighty main.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-62"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015025","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"36d6e41e1a4cf39b591f399f1f38d04e18e25b1124ba64258e2abf0b9a01a628","compact":"189d7ba80d659eb72418b0b7be2f532d236f0ee06844f3e5f543cfc102a061b5","nasal":"8e4c384de8b4c638d467bfbcde50838296790bd151340f4b4caf2def9808bca2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-26","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":26,"english":"And spacious, skilfully constructed, graceful, well-paved and nicely finished, the great bridge appeared like the line where the hair has been parted on the Ocean's head.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-63"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015026","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"39649ba83a658649bd88c9d2275d31858b93582066210be8ac5bf0b9f586b66b","compact":"101cb152731a8225485de8f421ff5471cd46a1a21d216b1f41e9689386f402ae","nasal":"6bc9af572705b7f85765d99759f24fa06ae13af0a5cf24e50c24de2a002c2f7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-27","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":27,"english":"Then on the other shore of the ocean, Bibhisbana with the view of opposing foes (that might advance), stationed himself mace in hand, along with some councilors.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.593,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-64"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015027","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1991038755e0474b63f54af3b86ef319d2789f9df70883e0b4768d30b97b4b14","compact":"34ea037ca66ce17a1f9e5621b1568b8ee329044f8117504143f94d0c6a2db450","nasal":"34ea037ca66ce17a1f9e5621b1568b8ee329044f8117504143f94d0c6a2db450"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-28","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":28,"english":"Thereat the graceful and righteous Rāma along with Laksmana, equipped with his bow, set out in the van of the army in company with Sugriva.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.779,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-66"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015028","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d73e9465f5bae8f6c6d1a8c58d4cdb95f12a4fa11f1b1973a9d2a0e21fc3c4a","compact":"12396600679151c5dff8d00221cffa3bb19b7b95556cc851f9bd961f879d2064","nasal":"12396600679151c5dff8d00221cffa3bb19b7b95556cc851f9bd961f879d2064"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-29","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":29,"english":"And some monkeys proceeded along the middle, and some plunged into the deep, and some went by the road. And some coursed through the air, bounding up bird-like.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.769,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-67"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015029","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"537d182b92a8f4e9c363d1ce0f3d9638a38f201fdc51a61a50e7aa518d5ded65","compact":"df3bfbce0774ee2452479940374abd4c2783ce35b8cf492aab7364d31aab6cc6","nasal":"4a6ec260ecebf815e6eb3ad0db4162446523e223cc4e53f67480799a917775ff"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-30","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":30,"english":"That dreadful array of monkeys crossing over, with its mighty uproar drowned the dreadful roar of the deep, which had been arising.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-68"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fece06b48d9da53fa00af257ceedd34f39facc72208e0dc13a9bdaa33725a4b7","compact":"71ed8cb57b2769f8a4e93213e8337504b99009326f13b527d8d09a5257a22729","nasal":"2688cb1b24dee8daf471fc3fd1b79988b228400da84ae09f556d7c52a5ea4f17"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-15-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":15,"verse":31,"english":"On the monkey-host having crossed by the bridge of Nala, the king stationed it on the shore abounding in fruits, roots, and water.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-22-69"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6015031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"28c703849d59774f5c67019b5e70688aa1f8315eafa38c966d9533719604045d","compact":"4380211a876673b3f95f26352e09306649391464d34c0b2c6a2582ee49d16307","nasal":"4380211a876673b3f95f26352e09